"{\"comments693\":[{\"id\":6589213896,\"url\":\"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/693#issuecomment\u002d6589213896\",\"body\":\"## Bounded T46 planning inputs \u2014 2026\u002d11\u002d02\\n\\nThe owner asked that existing M6 lanes continue useful milestone work. T43 is executing; T44 remains next and T46 remains last because earlier slices produce records. This is an immutable planning snapshot, not early T46 execution or a final membership recut.\\n\\nExisting **T3 wN:p6**, now available after accepted T41 completion, may derive a small cost/boundary report from P1 `2174265e9cc1b248c0fbe27fa101875984d46d6b` and frozen coordinator `92e8d07b6163ec5ddd3e9b67f1c42a472b2911d1`:\\n\\n1. Reconcile the recorded `records` selectors, 126,149 rows /22,984,582 inventory lines and the meaning of the generated read counts. Group by folder/type using existing inventory and Git mode/blob/size metadata; do not read millions of record lines to recreate a false code\u002dreview denominator.\\n2. Quantify frozen new/deleted/changed record\u002dpath metadata since P1, with concise group totals and exact commands. Distinguish the immutable survey population from later additions, source links and generated indexes. No live working\u002dtree scan.\\n3. Read only the specific plan/order sections, documentation/index conventions, D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d223/224 and #1407, plus current coordinator/T39 handoff references necessary to identify candidate entrypoints a stranger actually follows. Map ownership, historical\u002devidence retention, monthly\u002dindex backlog and the boundary with T39's completed reference corrections. Do not perform another audit or decide deletion/consolidation.\\n4. Return factual options for a bounded future T46 brief: which compact source inputs can bind membership, how to avoid recursive self\u002dcounting, and which costs can be measured from metadata versus require later proof. Root chooses scope, baseline, criteria and any action.\\n\\nUse small private text/JSON scratch and CPUs8\u201323. No full tree/export, audit\u002dlog body sweep, held/private directory or credential\u002dstore read, host/cache/process inspection, repository/tracker/kit write, cleanup, build/guest/runtime, fetch/provider/device/cloud action, accepted producer replay or permission answers. Historical T41 and launch trees remain untouched. Report exact pins/commands/hashes, limitations and useful next inputs to wN:p2, then stop.\\n\\nCan this be done on the VM? This is immutable Git/inventory planning metadata; no runtime behavior or new runtime allocation.\"},{\"id\":6602308433,\"url\":\"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/693#issuecomment\u002d6602308433\",\"body\":\"T46 final\u002dtable preparation \u2014 existing lanes resume in parallel, 2026\u002d11\u002d03\\n\\nT44 completion ad0df587 is verified under #691 comment6592382782. T46 is now next and remains the last source\u002dreading slice. Root is preparing its exact brief under plan \u00a7\u00a75/6b/7/8. These are bounded factual inputs, not the T46 audit, a recut, a removal decision or authority to change another lane.\\n\\nPrimary candidate source snapshot is immutable coordinator d707c82ab8c48b674acc1f95a9571f0cb24d226a. Stored survey at P1 2174265e9cc1b248c0fbe27fa101875984d46d6b still describes eb4763e3cc9bcd729830cd85f1719bbd4f28db10. Prior factual preparation at92e8d07b6163ec5ddd3e9b67f1c42a472b2911d1 is retained under docs/qa\u002dlogs/2026\u002d11\u002d02\u002dm6\u002dresume/t46\u002dpreparation/. Reuse it; do not rerun an accepted producer. Root will name survey/current additions, source cutoff and any separate accepted\u002dbranch context explicitly in the brief. No union of lane branches, no claim that this coordinator snapshot is integrated next, and no recursive counting of new outputs as their own input.\\n\\n**T3, wN:p6 \u2014 current metadata binding.** Read the existing retained report/deriver and this full owning issue. Compute only the new metadata transition92e8d07b\u2192d707c82 using unchanged records selectors, plus current path/mode/type/blob/size aggregates and identities. Reuse prior P1/survey counts; verify canonical inventory/areas/slices/generator identities still match. Cross\u002dcheck raw Git diff with two\u002dtree metadata; group additions/deletions/changes and logical bytes/unique blobs. Bind generated inventory self\u002drow as historical, not current content measurement. Return compact current digests/counts, exact argv and a reusable metadata\u002donly comparator; complete path sets stay in memory. No body sweep, final membership recut, own audit or baseline decision. Use absolute Git workdir /workspace/repos/pixelelated/distribution.worktrees/m6\u002drenovation\u002dplan\u002d346 read\u002donly, never edit T41 or historical trees.\\n\\n**P1, wN:p3 \u2014 bounded direct reader routes.** At d707c82 only, read the named entrypoints README.md, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .claude/rules/instruction\u002dfiles.md, docs/reviews/README.md, docs/audits/README.md, docs/retros/README.md, docs/futros/README.md, docs/work\u002dlogs/INDEX.md and .github/sessions/saved\u002dsession\u002dstate\u002dfeature\u002dm6\u002drenovation\u002dplan\u002d346.md. For the generated work\u002dlog INDEX, parse links/headers only; do not read its day bodies. Enumerate their literal direct repository\u002drelative references into the canonical records roots, retaining referring file/line, spelling, resolved path/anchor/line suffix and target Git mode/type/size/blob or missing. Distinguish external URLs, dynamic/glob examples, out\u002dof\u002dslice context and ambiguous syntax. Do not follow links recursively or read target audit/QA/log bodies. This is a finite factual input for root's reading floor, not a currency/link\u002daudit verdict. Return exact entrypoint identities, compact direct\u002dtarget grouping and a deterministic literal\u002dlink extractor with its syntax limits. No external fetching or target execution.\\n\\n**T1, wN:p4 \u2014 accepted T39 ownership bridge.** Reuse accepted T39 source4eb5dfab8e745914a55e7de3e5a43c5b91ebc608/completion7994f760fe1f4df6744844e80433bc49295cb94e, D229 and existing retained root acceptance/48\u002dsource\u002dpath outcomes. Compare only those named source/document identities with d707c82; report which accepted reference corrections are present or absent in the candidate snapshot. Read only the relevant already accepted disposition/source\u002dreference text needed to map current\u002dreader routes to existing owners; no re\u002dreview or rerun of T39. Preserve D223/D224/#1407's monthly\u002dindex and33\u002ddocument boundary. Return immutable path/identity/owner bridge and explicit integration\u002dpending qualifications; do not propose fixes/deletions, merge branch contents or select the final T46 reading set. Accepted work stays accepted.\\n\\nEach lane reads this complete issue/comment and uses CPUs8\u201323 for all subprocesses. Write only small private text/JSON report scratch; return the concise factual result with exact commands/hashes to wN:p2 and stop. Do not print/export credential\u002dlabelled paths or contents; retain bounded group counts/digests when such metadata occurs. No source/tree exports, private/held/cache/process/host inspection, repository/ledger/tracker/kit/shared\u002dref writes, generator/checker/test replay, cleanup, builds/guests/runtime, fetch/model\u002dprovider/device/cloud actions or permission answers. Historical worktrees stay untouched.\\n\\nRoot owns baseline, brief, criteria, epic/parent placement, stranger proof, acceptance and dispatch. T5 remains available for the later proved\u002dbrief handoff check; T2 available for subsequent bounded work. A successful preparation return does not start A\u2013D. Can this be done on the VM? No runtime is required: immutable metadata and explicitly named documentary inputs only.\"},{\"id\":6602413967,\"url\":\"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/693#issuecomment\u002d6602413967\",\"body\":\"T46 preparation clarification for P1 under 6602308433: the exact accepted records area selector excerpt at d707c82ab8c48b674acc1f95a9571f0cb24d226a is:\\n\\n```text\\ndocs/{qa\u002dlogs,qa\u002dframes,audits,work\u002dlogs,retros,retrospective,futros}/**\\nresearch/**\\n.github/sessions/**\\ndocs/reviews/inventory.json\\n```\\n\\nExpanded prefixes are docs/qa\u002dlogs/, docs/qa\u002dframes/, docs/audits/, docs/work\u002dlogs/, docs/retros/, docs/retrospective/, docs/futros/, research/, .github/sessions/, plus the exact singleton docs/reviews/inventory.json. Root verified the records entry of docs/reviews/areas.json. This supplies the requested excerpt; P1 need not open an eleventh source file. Keep literal spelling, anchors/line suffixes, ambiguity and target metadata separate. No target\u002dbody read, recursion or change to the bounded assignment.\\n\\nHerdr refused the prompt because a question UI was present; no interactive input or permission answer was sent. This comment is factual coordination, not audit dispatch.\"},{\"id\":6602867918,\"url\":\"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/693#issuecomment\u002d6602867918\",\"body\":\"T46 unfamiliar\u002dexecutor handoff proof \u2014 T5 wN:p7, bounded assignment.\\n\\nRead this full issue, records epic #1415, and candidate e9d512a230cf8dbd2cd985ae7984a6ef7eb9f9fc:docs/reviews/briefs/records.md. D236 and kickoff futro are committed; parent693\u21921415 is verified. Candidate is published clean. This is a handoff proof, not T46 audit/execution or a council verdict.\\n\\nIn at most ten top\u002dlevel commands, verify from a private scratch object clone with NO product/source checkout that the literal membership block works in one shell invocation and prints its exact expected result. Small ordinary helper/text/JSON files may be copied into that proof directory; no full tree export. Under /workspace/tmp for Git object clones/tiny Git, /tmp only for small text/JSON. CPU8\u201323 throughout; immutable source d707c82 and all historical trees stay unchanged.\\n\\nCheck: helper root\u002dtree and complete metadata binding, source/seed/output distinction; ten root totals127469/2190843187 and historical denominators; retained P1 five\u002doutput readback plus root selector join95occurrences/89targets; exact86 day\u002dlog range prescription, three other target kinds, templates/13shorthands/suppressed cases; accepted T39 bridge48 pre\u002dcorrection identities and #1407 boundary; real tool interfaces; actual Local\u002dlint model interface; output/criteria/stop/owner consistency. Root's seven in\u002dmemory binding negatives are not the executor's future table/link/confinement controls. Identify impossible/ambiguous predicates or missing literal inputs, not new audit findings.\\n\\nCheck source\u002dbinding refusals (including changed metadata, canonical input and empty\u002dsubtree root drift) and parser/selector limitations using metadata/tiny fixtures only. Do not read target historical day/audit/QA bodies or replay any accepted producer/parser/test/generator. Do not run final audit gates, scans, cleanup, integration, build/guest/runtime/provider/device/cloud actions or change any repository/tracker/shared kit/ref. Private new proof metadata only; no external fetch.\\n\\nPreserve the original P1 return and its selector\u002dpending wording: root's reader\u002droutes.json is a separate join. Its documentary TSV is stored reversibly as UTF\u002d8 JSON; p1\u002droutes/retention.json binds all14 original file bytes. The first candidate whitespace rc2 and later correction are separate; full tracked scan was0.\\n\\nReturn one concise proof report with exact commands, candidate/input hashes, pass/refusal results, concrete required corrections and explicit limits to root wN:p2, then stop. Root retains final brief/criteria/version, worktree/seed, dispatch and acceptance. T3 has not started A\u2013D.\"},{\"id\":6603284080,\"url\":\"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/693#issuecomment\u002d6603284080\",\"body\":\"T46 #693 \u2014 explicit A\u2013D execution dispatch to T3 wN:p6\\n\\nThe unfamiliar\u002dexecutor proof6602867918 is complete at candidate e9d512a230cf8dbd2cd985ae7984a6ef7eb9f9fc. Root has corrected all three concrete findings and verified the changes. Final v2 is immutable 647a8831739ffa28995e1955e68225ca0226c926:docs/reviews/briefs/records.md. Exact\u002dcommit refusal/positive, valid actual Local Epic JSON and seven new deterministic day\u002drange cases are retained under docs/qa\u002dlogs/2026\u002d11\u002d03\u002dm6\u002drecords\u002dpreparation/. New required record/issue gates pass. Original v1 behavior, two proof\u002dreader failures and whitespace refusal remain historical evidence.\\n\\nProceed now, continuously through A\u2013D, in this exact new checkout:\\n\u002d worktree /workspace/repos/pixelelated/distribution.worktrees/m6\u002drecords\u002d693\\n\u002d branch feature/m6\u002drecords\u002d693\\n\u002d clean published execution seed 8710a6210a40de0110244d03a886161ee06faf29\\n\u002d seed parent / governing v2 coordinator 647a8831739ffa28995e1955e68225ca0226c926\\n\u002d source cutoff d707c82ab8c48b674acc1f95a9571f0cb24d226a, root tree b3ce6c6ea70d9d40ff2b74fff691a0a11f70e437\\n\u002d initial pointer .github/sessions/saved\u002dsession\u002dstate\u002dfeature\u002dm6\u002drecords\u002d693.md\\n\\nHEAD=remote and empty status were verified after normal commit/push. Actual #693 parent is records epic #1415 in M6; current18criteria match the final brief. Source reviewed\u002dat and execution\u002dseed are separate fields, fixed\u002dat remains empty.\\n\\nRead the full current owning issue, this dispatch, #1415/futro and v2/current rules before acting. Record actual observed harness/model/effort; normalize the lint model as the supplied Local JSON specifies, without provider attestation. Verify actual seed/branch/clean state, run the literal source\u002dbinding block once for your new Stage A, and proceed without intermediate approval gates. First independent reader observations precede accepted verdict comparison.\\n\\nNative/current metadata and source cutoff remain distinct from future outputs. Current127469 paths are folder\u002dtable coverage, not a full historical reading. Execute only v2's ten\u002dentrypoint/95\u002droute89\u002dtarget reading floor, with exact day\u002drange metadata,120\u002dline cap/40\u002dline unknown fallback and honest unread/masked limits. Previous preparation no\u002dtarget\u002dbody restrictions applied to that preparation; this dispatch authorizes the new v2 bounded readings. New audit\u002dlocal table/link/confinement controls remain your duties; preparatory helper proof is not an audit verdict.\\n\\nWrite only the named audit root docs/audits/2026_11_03\u002depic\u002dm6\u002drecords/, exact lane pointer and actual\u002ddate log/INDEX as permitted. No product fix/removal/relocation, historical record rewrite, accepted audit/test/generator/application replay, branch union, source export, fetch, build/guest/runtime, provider/device/cloud/host action or permission answer. All subprocesses CPUs8\u201323; historical emulator/T41 trees untouched. Accepted T39 remains accepted with #686/#807/#346 integration pending; #1407 monthly\u002dindex/33\u002dreference work remains separate.\\n\\nReturn substantive progress or an early concrete blocker. At D, file the genuine audit child/any nonduplicate reactive bugs under the stated boundaries, complete06/07 and exact readbacks, then publish one clean D packet and STOP for root stream disposition. Do not start E, select Phase7 outcomes, close the audit/slice or write a completion marker. Root retains acceptance, future stream brief, integration and closure.\"},{\"id\":6603680264,\"url\":\"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/693#issuecomment\u002d6603680264\",\"body\":\"T46 A/B progress received from T3 wN:p6, 2026\u002d11\u002d03 12:22 UTC. Actual reported primary: Codex/GPT\u002d6\u002dAstra/xhigh, session01a19d12\u002d29e3\u002d7fe0\u002d9f41\u002d038dac0a5deb.\\n\\nThe executor reports new literal Stage\u002dA binding PASS:127469 paths/2190843187 logical bytes/ten roots; seed8710a621 remains distinct from sourced707c82. Nine prose entrypoints, INDEX headings/links and all86 normative day ranges have individual observations; historical next\u002dpointer status/navigation is separately bounded. New Local positive and reviewer\u002dcount refusal pass, while first incomplete\u002dfixture failures remain preserved. Independent observations preceded accepted T39 comparison; the48 accepted corrections and #1407 ownership remain intact.\\n\\nAudit\u002dlocal table/link/history controls and A\u2013D synthesis are next. The docs/audits/README.md:19 applyTo wording is a lead undergoing duplicate\u002downer checking, not a confirmed new bug or a source\u002dfix assignment. Records are currently uncommitted in the assigned audit root. Root has not inspected moving producer files or independently accepted these reported results.\\n\\nDispatch6603284080 continues unchanged: no intermediate approval gate; return a concrete blocker or one clean published D packet, then stop for root stream disposition. No source change, old producer replay or runtime action is reported.\"},{\"id\":6603822870,\"url\":\"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/693#issuecomment\u002d6603822870\",\"body\":\"T46 Stage\u002dC progress received from T3 wN:p6, 2026\u002d11\u002d03 12:29 UTC; actual reported primary Codex/GPT\u002d6\u002dAstra/xhigh, session01a19d12\u002d29e3\u002d7fe0\u002d9f41\u002d038dac0a5deb.\\n\\nThe executor reports all finite95\u002droute/89\u002dtarget readings complete with99 total entrypoint/target rows, explicit masks/fallbacks and86/86 day\u002dindex counts aligned. New table positive passes and8 independent mutations refuse (the7 required categories, with duplicate and omitted rows tested separately). Path/anchor positive and negatives behave as required; the per\u002dcommit guard rejects source edit and edit\u002dthen\u002drevert.\\n\\nOne open Low documentation finding is reported: docs/audits/README.md:19 uses applyTo where the named rule convention is paths. The bounded T39/issue duplicate check found no existing owner for this defect. Root has not yet verified the final immutable finding/evidence packet; no source edit or Phase7 outcome is selected.\\n\\nT3 continues exact D issue filing/readbacks and normal publication under6603284080, then stops at one clean published D packet for root disposition. Source d707c82 and execution seed8710 remain separate. All18 criteria remain unchecked; no intermediate acceptance or additional approval gate is introduced.\"},{\"id\":6604179796,\"url\":\"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/693#issuecomment\u002d6604179796\",\"body\":\"T46 Stage D \u2014 clean published handback; STOPPED for root stream disposition.\\n\\nActual primary: Codex / GPT\u002d6\u002dAstra / xhigh, T3 m6\u002dt3\u002demulators wN:p6, session01a19d12\u002d29e3\u002d7fe0\u002d9f41\u002d038dac0a5deb. Observed harness identity, not provider\u002dattested. Local reviewers[], D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d184; no external reviewer/provider call.\\n\\nPublished tip **a0d4c4fda7a0c16c04d57edf921ffeb741eff19b**, tree05c9988bbee9a9341fedc26eb33bcba698b781bd, exact worktree /workspace/repos/pixelelated/distribution.worktrees/m6\u002drecords\u002d693, branch feature/m6\u002drecords\u002d693. Normal commit and push exited0; live ls\u002dremote equals this full tip and porcelain status is empty. Execution seed8710a6210a40de0110244d03a886161ee06faf29 remains separate from source cutoffd707c82ab8c48b674acc1f95a9571f0cb24d226a/rootb3ce6c6ea70d9d40ff2b74fff691a0a11f70e437. Governing v2 is647a8831739ffa28995e1955e68225ca0226c926. fixed\u002dat remains empty pending disposition/acceptance.\\n\\nPacket: [00\u201307 and evidence](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/tree/a0d4c4fda7a0c16c04d57edf921ffeb741eff19b/docs/audits/2026_11_03\u002depic\u002dm6\u002drecords), [summary](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/blob/a0d4c4fda7a0c16c04d57edf921ffeb741eff19b/docs/audits/2026_11_03\u002depic\u002dm6\u002drecords/06\u002daudit\u002dsummary.md), [punch list](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/blob/a0d4c4fda7a0c16c04d57edf921ffeb741eff19b/docs/audits/2026_11_03\u002depic\u002dm6\u002drecords/05\u002dpunch\u002dlist.md), exact lane pointer and dated log/INDEX updated.\\n\\nSubstantive result:\\n\u002d Ten exhaustive metadata roots:127469 paths/2190843187 logical bytes;38355 unique blobs/1084128032 unique\u002dblob logical bytes. Historical126149 rows/22984582 stored lines, CODE15392661 and inventory self\u002drow134637 remain distinct. Retained799A/0D/4M delta reused; no generator replay or disk\u002dsavings claim.\\n\u002d Ten entrypoints,95 route occurrences/89 distinct targets,99 bounded reading records.71 timestamp sections/15 prescribed unknown\u002dformat fallbacks; no selected section truncated. Masks and unread bodies explicit.86/86 INDEX counts align; all heading metadata retained without body credit.13 shorthands remain unresolved;8 sensitive\u002dlabelled occurrences stay suppressed counts/digest only.\\n\u002d Complete new table positive passes;8 independent mutations refuse (all7 required categories, duplicate/omission separately). New path/anchor positive, missing target/anchor refusals and unsupported\u002dsyntax unknown retained. Per\u002dcommit guard rejects source edits and edit\u002dthen\u002drevert, and passes the actual one\u002dcommit seed\u2192D history. Actual Local positive\u002dv2 and reviewer\u002dcount refusal pass intended predicates; initial incomplete fixture failures preserved.\\n\u002d **One Low PL\u002d001**, no Critical/High/Medium: current audit README:19 uses applyTo where canonical rule selection is paths/every\u002dsession. Literal trace, consequence, self\u002drefu