d nonblocking ceremony warning remain preserved.29 D files use lossless JSON transport: stored bytes and decoded original\u002dstream identities are separate. All305 frozen D files and17 original tools remain unchanged and unexecuted during E\u2013H.\\n\\nRoot/P1 reconciliation qualifies D rather than rewriting it: first pre\u002dissue04/05 inputs are8278/2482\u002dbyte prefixes, not8920/2807 final bytes; pre\u002dseal00/06 are3846/3946 prefixes, not5007/5107. Later D issue lint does not explicitly bind final04/05 inputs. Forty outside\u002daudit input occurrences were not independently reopened by support. Current child\u002dscript hashes cannot repair historical bindings. New F runs retain full current04/05/plan/README/checker input snapshots, command times/exits and exact stream bytes separately.\\n\\nDated factual errata correct95 occurrences/89 unique targets and reviewed\u002dsource context17\u201320, finding19. Original D source/readbacks remain immutable. The small current correction is not a rewrite of historical commands or authorship.\\n\\n## Guard lesson\\n\\nA clean net working diff does not prove the staged index is safe. The new E\u2013H guard independently checks every commit, index mode/blob identities, working changes, untracked paths and305 frozen identities.13 relevant refusals and a complete positive include unauthorized source/frozen/wrong\u002dREADME bytes staged while working files are restored, edit\u002dthen\u002drevert, wrong README followed by repair, unrelated dates, executable/symlink/merge/deletion states. Tiny fixture working files are retained; the deletion case removes only a synthetic index entry and leaves its file.\\n\\nThe first new guard positive failed because it conflated POSIX0664 permissions with Git\u2019s non\u002dexecutable100644 mode. Its original program/outputs remain. Corrected v2 uses the actual Git distinction; all final refusal cases are isolated from that false failure. No D producer/control was replayed. Procedure is captured in separately named eh\u002d* tools and new stage\u002de/f/g/h records.\\n\\n## Instruction File Recommendations\\n\\nThis fixes a reference to an existing instruction\u002dselection rule. It does not justify another global rule, registry change or duplicated policy. Exact current\u002dinput snapshots and separate index inspection are implemented in the new local evidence tools; root retains global rule/register decisions.\\n\\n## Retention and next owner\\n\\nH is retained\u002donly. Its bounded census covers only the two named D\u002downed roots and new E\u2013H tiny fixture root, using no\u002dfollow traversal and current identities/counts. No historical inode/creation/process evidence is invented; inaccessible entries remain retained with limitations. Ordinary D and E\u2013H publication packets are separately named and retained. Nothing is deleted, no global /tmp/host/process/cache scan occurs, and no held/unrelated directory is opened. Root owns any later retirement decision, exact\u002dtip simulation, final acceptance, marker and ordered integration.\\n\\nNo source edit beyond the specified paragraph, source acquisition/export, package/config evaluation, old producer replay, merge, runtime/build/guest/provider/device/cloud/host\u002dledger action or permission answer. All subprocesses/children CPUs8\u201323. G/H and final publication proceed under the existing dispatch without an approval relay.\\n\"},{\"id\":6605414149,\"url\":\"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/693#issuecomment\u002d6605414149\",\"body\":\"T46 final S1/E\u2013H handback \u2014 clean published 17a064e6110306dd2b692cfd1b13d4f518d8def5; stop for root acceptance.\\n\\nActual primary: Codex / GPT\u002d6\u002dAstra / xhigh (observed harness, not provider\u002dattested), Local reviewers[], T3 m6\u002dt3\u002demulators wN:p6, session 01a19d12\u002d29e3\u002d7fe0\u002d9f41\u002d038dac0a5deb. Executed under full comment 6604790499 and immutable stream v2 at 2aea545afb74